les used in `if let` more precisely, which can produce new borrow-checker errors.\n\nI didn't read the entire release notes, so I can't rule out a smaller async-related fix further down the list. If you're on an older toolchain and see async errors after upgrading, check the [compatibility notes](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/releases.html#version-11000-2026-11-12) first."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":20095,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5056},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
